      "id": "counterpoint-independent-melodic-lines",
      "title": "Counterpoint: Independent Melodic Lines",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** harmony | **Difficulty:** 9/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Counterpoint combines melodies so each line remains intelligible while harmonising together."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "species-counterpoint",
      "title": "Species counterpoint",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Gradus ad Parnassum tradition: stepwise motion, consonance on strong beats, careful dissonance treatment. Foundation for Bach fugues."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "motion-types",
      "title": "Motion types",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Contrary**: voices move opposite directions. **Parallel**: same direction. **Oblique**: one holds, other moves. Contrary and oblique preserve independence."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "in-trad",
      "title": "In trad",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Pipe regulators, harp bass, twin-fiddle harmony. Lines need not share rhythm. Sing each line alone — if it sounds random, simplify."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
